## Report
Rubric-guided validation with dynamic repro. Crash attempt: ran `cargo test -p auth --test policy_bypass -- --nocapture` (debug build); no crash since issue is logic. Valgrind attempt: `valgrind --version` not available. Debugger attempt: `gdb --version` not available.

Code evidence: In `crates/auth/src/bucket_policy.rs`, `condition_clause_matches_request` maps `aws:PrincipalArn` and `aws:SourceVpc` to `ConditionMatchResult::AcceptedButNotEvaluable` (lines 1278-1291). In `PolicyStatement::request_effect`, `AcceptedButNotEvaluable` returns `None`, meaning the statement is ignored even for Deny (lines 549-566). This skips deny statements that rely on these conditions, allowing other allow statements/ACLs to grant access.

Dynamic PoC: added integration test `crates/auth/tests/policy_bypass.rs` that builds a policy with a Deny on `aws:PrincipalArn` plus a blanket Allow. Running `cargo test -p auth --test policy_bypass -- --nocapture` prints `evaluation: ExplicitAllow`, confirming the Deny is ignored and Allow wins. Output captured in `/workspace/validation_artifacts/policy_bypass/policy_bypass_output.txt` (also inside the tarball).

